+*   **When Not to Use:** For simple scenes or when real-time initialization is required without pre-training [G].
 
 ## Background
-SF-VAE was introduced in the unofficial repository `cilix-ai/gs-embedding` [S1, unofficial]. It is part of the family of learning-based initialization methods for 3D Gaussian Splatting, aiming to improve reconstruction quality by leveraging neural networks to predict Gaussian parameters from a latent space.
+SF-VAE originates from the `gs-embedding` project, an unofficial implementation [S1, unofficial]. It is designed to integrate with Gaussian Splatting pipelines to improve the initial placement and parameterization of Gaussians [S1, unofficial]. The method leverages the spherical folding technique to decode latent representations into 3D geometry [S1, unofficial].
 
